Decode archive entry names as UTF-8 when extracting

"extract" builds each output path from an entry's archived name by
constructing std::filesystem::path from the plain std::string. mpqcli stores
those names as UTF-8 (WindowsifyFilePath uses u8string()). libstdc++ decodes
a narrow path as UTF-8, but libc++ decodes it in the ANSI code page, so on
clang64 an entry with a non-ASCII name was written under a garbled local name
while ucrt64 got it right. Use fs::u8path for the three constructions, which
reads UTF-8 with either library -- what ucrt64 already did.

Command-line paths are a different matter: they reach main() in the ANSI code
page, and 0002's StormArgPath converts those.

Upstream: not submitted yet
Applies-to: all environments (the failure shows on clang64)

